From 9f513b853d540ae8429d27030f86e155f6a2b98f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wujian Sun <wujian.sun_1@nxp.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Sep 2025 10:08:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] MGS-7765: Blacklist MSAA for GPU Raster on Vivante GPUs

Vivante had poor performance when enbale MSAA, disable MSAA
for Vivante GPU.

The same workaround as other GPU vendor having the same issue.
https://codereview.chromium.org/1374043005

Upstream-Status: Pending

Change-Id: I7e562f29fb3039fe3c0e1ee36c04e7d8e8c10b37
Signed-off-by: Wujian Sun <wujian.sun_1@nxp.com>
---
 gpu/config/gpu_driver_bug_list.json | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gpu/config/gpu_driver_bug_list.json b/gpu/config/gpu_driver_bug_list.json
index 34b654ecebc28..4995df50d4e17 100644
--- a/gpu/config/gpu_driver_bug_list.json
+++ b/gpu/config/gpu_driver_bug_list.json
@@ -3514,6 +3514,17 @@
         "op": ">",
         "value": "32.0.101.6078"
       }
+    },
+    {
+       "id": 448,
+       "description": "On Vivante GPUs MSAA performance is not acceptable for GPU rasterization",
+       "os": {
+         "type": "linux"
+       },
+       "gl_vendor": "Vivante Corporation",
+       "features": [
+         "msaa_is_slow"
+       ]
     }
   ]
 }
